# File size limit (Noni)

Hard max **200 lines** per `.cpp` / `.hpp` (comments and blank lines count). Generated/data tables also split by category — no 200+ exceptions.

## When adding or editing code

- If a file is already **>200 lines**, extract by **feature** (same class OK across translation units).
- Do **not** grow god-files (`ui.cpp`, `editor.cpp`, `lsp_service.cpp`) — put new methods in the matching split file (see `PROGRESS.md` T2).
- If an edit would push a file over 200, split in the **same task**.
- Split = cut/paste + `make`; no drive-by refactors. Split commit = pure move, no feature/bugfix mix. One source file split per commit.

## Pattern

```text
includes/foo/bar.hpp     ← declarations
src/foo/bar.cpp          ← core
src/foo/bar_feature.cpp  ← UI::feature_* or Bar::feature_*
```

Internal helpers: anonymous namespace or `*_detail.hpp`. Public API/behavior stays the same.

## Tracking

Queue and file list: repo-root `PROGRESS.md`. After a planned split, mark that T2 item done there.
